 @slayerr4365  Because AMD isn't "leaps and bounds better" than Nvidia at this point.

If the GPU doesn't sell, the board partners have to pay Nvidia from their coffers. Earlier, it used to be  something like Nvidia gets 60% of the "final price" so board partners could settle for ~80% of the price for the cards and 100% of it for premium cards. Now Nvidia has not only locked the minimum price, it also makes it's own cards and sells for ~10% less to ~10% more than the locked price which makes Nvidia manufactured cards a "lucrative deal".

There's no point in "joining the Nvidia family" if they treat you like an adopted kid and they would've lost a shit load of money if they remained for this skew just like all board partners have. A lot of them are going to complain and/or quit after this one.

